// The values stage's outputs (values.dl), derived once and read as facts.
// Included by imports.dl; FlowLog prunes them from a program that reads
// none, and only an analysis that reads one waits on the stage.
//
// Positions are spelled as term-flow spells a parameter variable ("0").

// Literal `value` may be what parameter `pos` of the program's function
// `func` holds, from some caller, through any chain of callers passing it
// on unchanged.
.decl param_value(func: symbol, pos: symbol, value: symbol) mutable
.input param_value

// Every value parameter `pos` of `func` may hold is a param_value: every
// caller is seen, and each hands a literal or a parameter whose own set
// is complete. A parameter with no row may hold a value no literal names.
.decl param_complete(func: symbol, pos: symbol) mutable
.input param_complete

// `caller` hands the program's function `callee` the literal `value` at
// `pos`: its own literal, or one the parameter it passes on, or a result
// it hands on, may hold.
.decl arg_value(caller: symbol, callee: symbol, pos: symbol, value: symbol) mutable
.input arg_value

// Every value `caller` hands `callee` at `pos` is an arg_value.
.decl arg_complete(caller: symbol, callee: symbol, pos: symbol) mutable
.input arg_complete

// Literal `value` reaches parameter `pos` of `func` from the call at
// `site` in `caller`, which spells it (or hands on a result holding it),
// through any chain of calls passing it on unchanged: the caller a rule
// credits the value to.
.decl param_origin(func: symbol, pos: symbol, caller: symbol, site: symbol, value: symbol) mutable
.input param_origin

// Which values program wrote the relations: "full", or "unknown" when
// the full one outgrew its budget and none of the relations above has a
// row.
.decl values_mode(mode: symbol) mutable
.input values_mode
